  "id": "V014",
  "description": "Tie at the finalist boundary broken by rung 1 of the chain: higher approval",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 1 / Selecting finalists: 'Ties at the finalist boundary (e.g. 5th and 6th place with equal yes-votes) are common in a small group and must be broken deterministically, never by insertion order. Reuse the runoff's chain: higher approval, then rotation fairness, then shortest runtime, then seeded random.'",
  "rationale": "N_FINALISTS is set to 2 so the boundary is between 2nd and 3rd place. 5 attendees. m1: 5 rows, 4 yes -> coverage 1.00, yes 4, approval 0.80. m2: 3 rows (u1,u2 yes; u3 no) -> coverage 3/5 = 0.60 (at floor), yes 2, approval 2/3 = 0.6667. m3: 4 rows (u1,u2 yes; u3,u4 no) -> coverage 0.80, yes 2, approval 2/4 = 0.50. All three are eligible and all three clear APPROVAL_FLOOR. Ranking by yes-votes: m1 = 4 takes slot 1; m2 and m3 both have 2 yes-votes and there is one slot left -> boundary tie. Rung 1 approval: m2 0.6667 > m3 0.50 -> m2 admitted, m3 excluded. Runoff over {m1,m2}: m1 preferred 3 (u1,u2,u3) to 2 (u4,u5) -> m1 beats every other finalist = Condorcet winner.",
